    whatsReallyGoingOn: "Most people don't actually forget names — they never registered them, because they were busy being nervous. Remembering is a skill, not a talent, and using someone's name back is one of the warmest things you can do. People feel genuinely valued when you recall the small stuff about their life.",
    whatToSay: ["\"Sarah — nice to meet you, Sarah.\"","\"Sorry, say that one more time? I want to get it right.\"","\"Marcus — like the planet? Got it.\" (make a tiny mental tag)","\"I'm so sorry — remind me of your name? I'm terrible with this and I'd rather just ask.\"","\"Help me out — we met at the game, right? I'm blanking on your name.\"","\"How'd your daughter's recital go? You mentioned it last time.\"","\"Did you ever sort out that work trip?\""],
