    whatsReallyGoingOn: "Adult friendships almost never form on their own anymore; somebody has to make the small, slightly-brave move from \"we talk at pickup\" to \"let's actually hang out.\" Most parents want more friends and are waiting for someone else to suggest it. Being the one who suggests it is a gift, not an imposition.",
    whatToSay: ["\"The kids clearly love each other — want to do a playdate this weekend?\"","\"We're going to the park Saturday, you guys should come.\"","\"Want to grab a coffee sometime, just us? No kids for once.\"","\"We should get the adults together for once — drinks Friday?\"","\"Let me get your number so we can plan it.\"","\"I'll text you — what works better, weekends or weeknights?\""],
