    whatsReallyGoingOn: "Group conversations have a rhythm, and the people who speak up aren't bolder — they've just learned to claim the entry, not wait for a perfect silence (which never comes). A short signal that you want to talk reserves your spot. And once you're in, briefer is better; long contributions lose the room.",
    whatToSay: ["\"Can I jump in here?\"","\"I'd like to add one thing.\"","\"Before we move on — quick point.\"","\"I didn't quite finish my thought — one second.\"","\"Let me circle back to what I was saying.\"","\"To build on what [name] said…\"","\"Yeah, and one thing I'd add…\""],
