    title: "Having Honest Conversations",
    theMoment: "You tend to soften, dodge, or avoid the full truth to keep the peace — and you want to be able to say what you really think and feel, honestly but kindly.",
    whatsReallyGoingOn: "Honesty and kindness aren't opposites — the skill is being truthful without being harsh, which most people never learn because they think the choice is \"nice lie\" or \"brutal truth.\" Real honesty, delivered with care, deepens trust and respect. People can handle the truth when they can feel that you're saying it for the relationship, not against them.",
    whatToSay: ["\"Can I be totally honest with you? I care enough to be straight.\"","\"I'm going to be real with you, because you deserve that from me.\"","\"Here's the honest version — and I'm saying it gently because I mean it kindly.\"","\"I'd be lying if I said [X], and I'd rather be honest with you.\"","\"I want us to be able to tell each other the truth.\"","\"You can be just as honest back — I'd rather that than polite.\""],
    questionsToAsk: ["\"Do you want the honest answer or the easy one?\"","\"Can we agree to be real with each other?\"","\"What's the truth you're not saying?\""],
